# Tailwind CSS v4 Design & Styling Rules

## Styling Standards
- Adhere to the established design system color tokens (e.g., Slate background `#030712`, Emerald accents `#10B981`).
- Avoid arbitrary values (e.g., `w-[347px]`, `top-[13px]`) unless strictly required by pixel-exact vector specs.
- Ensure all interactive elements (buttons, links, inputs) have accessible focus rings (`focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-emerald-400`).
- Ensure contrast ratios satisfy WCAG AAA standards for all body copy and secondary labels.
- Structure responsive class names systematically: mobile-first base classes, followed by `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`, `xl:`.
